---
/**
 * /legal/terms — the companion to the privacy page (§8.3).
 *
 * Written to be honest about a free, in-development game rather than to be
 * maximally protective: the save-loss warning and the "this is unfinished"
 * statement are the two things a player actually needs to know before they
 * invest hours.
 *
 * Not legal advice, and it says so.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site, socials } from "../../lib/site";

const updated = "27 August 2026";
const github = socials().find((s) => s.id === "github");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms"
  pathname="/legal/terms/"
  description="Terms for using Isoperia: free, in development, provided as-is, and your saves live on your device."
>
  <section class="doc">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2 id="short">The short version</h2>
        <p>
          {site.name} is free, unfinished, and provided as-is. Your saves live in your browser
          and can be lost. Play it, enjoy it, do not rely on it.
        </p>

        <h2 id="free">It is free, and there is nothing to buy</h2>
        <p>
          There is no purchase, no subscription, no currency, and no advertising. Nothing
          on this site or in the game takes payment, and nothing ever asks for card
          details. If you encounter something that does, it is not us.
        </p>

        <h2 id="development">It is in development</h2>
        <p>
          The game is actively being built and the devlog documents that honestly,
          including the regressions. Systems change, content is replaced, and behaviour
          that works today may be reworked. Nothing here is a commitment to a feature, a
          date, or a final design.
        </p>

        <h2 id="saves">Saves can be lost</h2>
        <p>
          This is the one that matters. Saves are stored only in your browser. Clearing
          site data, browsing privately, switching browser or device, or a browser
          deciding to evict storage will lose your progress, and there is no server-side
          copy to restore from because there is no server.
        </p>
        <p>
          The game can export a save to a file. Use it. We cannot recover a lost save for
          you.
        </p>

        <h2 id="asis">Provided as-is</h2>
        <p>
          The game and this site are provided without warranty of any kind, to the extent
          permitted by law. They may be unavailable, may contain faults, and may lose
          data. Do not use them for anything that matters beyond playing a game.
        </p>

        <h2 id="conduct">Reasonable use</h2>
        <p>
          Please do not attempt to disrupt the site for other people, or redistribute the
          game embedded in a page that misrepresents its origin. The site sends headers
          that prevent it being framed elsewhere, which is the same request in
          machine-readable form.
        </p>
        <p>
          Modifying your own save file is explicitly fine — the game ships import and
          export, so it is a feature rather than a loophole. There are no leaderboards, so
          there is nothing to be unfair to.
        </p>

        <h2 id="ip">Ownership and third-party work</h2>
        <p>
          The game's code, art, and writing belong to the project except where noted. Some
          shipped assets are third-party work used under CC0 — a Poly Haven terrain
          texture and a subset of Kenney's Fantasy Town Kit. Every shipped asset's owner,
          source, and licence status is recorded. Both CC0 sources are named here in full
          because CC0 asks for attribution even where it does not require it.
        </p>
        {
          github && (
            <p>
              The source is public:{" "}
              <a href={github.url} rel="noopener noreferrer">
                {github.url}
              </a>
              . Its licence, where one is stated, governs the code.
            </p>
          )
        }

        <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may change as the project does. The date at the top will change with
          them.
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          <p>
            This page is written to be clear rather than to be legally comprehensive, and
            it has not been reviewed by a lawyer. It should be reviewed before the project
            takes payment, collects personal data, or launches publicly at scale.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doc {
    padding-block: var(--space-3xl) var(--space-4xl);
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    margin-top: var(--space-2xs);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }
</style>
